        "like": 2
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I’m dealing with this issue too. Been troubleshooting and testing all day on an old commission I’m reworking just to realize that it seems like every avatar I’ve updated over the past week now suffers from this weird animation issue. Seems like applying custom animations to gestures is the cause of it, two of the 4 avatars I’ve tested only have custom gestures on the left hand (facial animations, mainly blendshapes but some non humanoid bone animation as well) and thus only the left hand seems to be effected. Uncertain of the cause but I’ve tried using an older version of the sdk that the only avatar I’ve updated that is completely unaffected by this issue runs on but it remains unaffected regardless of current or older sdk version which is odd.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "6322bf8b5eba5044ab484962",
      "author": {
        "_id": "6277618ec39b16529db00df1",
        "alias": "Apparent Antelope",
        "aliasID": "65d911220129d7ae44032933",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": null,
        "created": "2022-05-08T06:22:06.206Z",
        "name": "LittleBirdy",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "5d09629c3511d825c8e56214",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2022-09-15T06:00:43.466Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "631d8209c6677b44b7961eef",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 4
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The issue is only present in the latest SDK.\n-Whenever your state transitions to a animation that is animating the animator it breaks the hand gestures \n-The parameters and states still transition correctly but the hands kinda get stuck open\n-The animation can be triggered by anything in the FX controller not necessarily the gesture parameter or layer and break the hand\n-The animation doesn't have to animate the hand but rather the animator in general\n-Turning write defaults OFF seems to fix it\n-Getting rid of animations that animates the animator fixes it\n-*Turns out the problem can also be solved by removing the mask for the FX controller layer for the Hand\nTypically, booth avatars have write defaults ON and have an idle state with an idle animation with the animator being animated \n(So it pretty much instantly breaks since the issue is the idle animation and write defaults)\nI could provide a visual example or reference if necessary. \n(Just tell me what you need to see)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
